# Language-model drafting for report-card comments — entirely optional.
#
# With no key set, the app works exactly as it does today: comments are drafted
# by the structured on-device drafter and nothing leaves the building. The
# "Inspect what would be sent" button still works without a key, so you can
# review the payload before deciding anything.
#
# Set this in your hosting provider's environment settings (Vercel: Project →
# Settings → Environment Variables). Do NOT commit a real key to the repo.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5.
ANTHROPIC_COMMENT_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MCP server (/api/mcp) — also optional, and off unless this is set.
#
# Lets a teacher drive the LMS from whatever assistant they already use:
# "which of my Chem 11 students haven't demonstrated CC-3 yet?"
#
# THE TOKEN IS THE IDENTITY. Each entry is `token:teacherId`, and the token is
# how the server knows which teacher is calling — the caller never states it.
# A shared token plus a teacherId argument would let anyone holding the token
# read any teacher's class by changing one parameter.
#
# Generate real random tokens; the examples below are illustrative only.
#   LMS_MCP_TOKENS=sk-lab-8f3c...:t-rivera,sk-lab-2a91...:t-tan
#
# Static bearer tokens suit a sandbox of invented students. A real deployment
# wants the MCP authorization framework (OAuth 2.1) against the portal's own
# identity provider, so access is revocable, attributable and expiring.
LMS_MCP_TOKENS=
